<title>SOUTH AFRICA: STEERS RAISES YR SHR, DIV INCREASED.</title>
<headline>STEERS RAISES YR SHR, DIV INCREASED.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended February 28</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     14.51     vs    11.16</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		   7.5     vs    5.5  </p>
<p>    Attrib income	    7.60     vs    5.83</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   12.28     vs    10.10</p>
<p>    Tax			  4.72     vs    4.23 </p>
<p>    Interest recieved	0.17     vs    0.56</p>
<p>    Turnover		 103.99     vs    84.77</p>
<p>Div payable June 6</p>
<p>on register May 30</p>
<p>Full name: Steers Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it listed &quot;N&quot; shares in the year</p>
<p>under review and the financial results relate to the increased</p>
<p>number of shares in issue. It said the comparatives were also</p>
<p>referred to in terms of the altered share capital.</p>
<p>International operations of the group which were currently</p>
<p>limited to Africa and Mauritius were new growth areas for the</p>
<p>business.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
